  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nConsider the following code:\n\n```javascript\nclass MyElement extends HTMLElement { }\ncustomElements.define(\"a-a:a\", MyElement);\n```\n\nPer [Section 4.13.3](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#custom-elements-core-concepts) of Custom Elements, I believe that this is a valid name. There is nothing prohibiting the `:` character, which is allowed per [Section 1.4](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#namespaces).\n\nFirefox allows the custom element to be registered, Safari and Chrome throw `SyntaxError: Custom element name contains a character that is not allowed`.\n\nShould Section 4.13.3 explicitly prohibit the `:` character?\n\n",
